Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/opencontainers/runc v1.5.3

H-4 of the runc series: Create and Load build the cgroup v2 manager directly.
Upstream calls manager.New and manager.NewWithPaths of
github.com/opencontainers/cgroups/manager, and factory_linux.go is the only
file of libcontainer that imports that package. The package links the systemd
cgroup driver and the cgroup v1 manager, neither of which a ze appliance can
use: it has no systemd and runs the unified hierarchy.

newCgroupV2Manager keeps the checks manager.NewWithPaths made (a nil config,
the shape of the saved path) and refuses what it no longer builds: a config
that asks for the systemd driver, and a host that is not in cgroup v2 unified
mode.

No upstream pull request is opened for this change: upstream selects the
manager at run time on purpose. The design is
docs/architecture/container/runtime.md.

Delete this series when Ze no longer vendors the runtime.

